# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## Grounding unified and surface classification introduced

**What**

`CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction` reshaped: `MinDeltaDegrees` → `FlatSnapDegrees`, `MaxDeltaDegrees` →
`MaxAngleDelta: { Ground: 35, Sliding: 60 }`.

Surfaces are now classified as `"walkable" | "sliding" | "wall"` by a pure `classifySurface`, from the
angle between a persistent `referenceNormal` and the candidate normal plus the candidate's absolute
incline. The result is published on `entity.surfaceContact`; `resetSurfaceState` writes `"none"` and
takes the contact as an argument. `angleBetweenDegrees` replaces two inline degree conversions.

`referenceNormal` holds the last walked surface normal. `frameStart` snapshots it for the frame, and it
is written once after the correction loop — to the current `surfaceNormal` when the contact is
`"walkable"` and position changed, to world up when the contact is `"none"`.

Grounding is now derived rather than assigned: `ResolveGrounded(entity)` is the single authority and the
six other `grounded` writers were deleted. `shouldSkipJumpGrounding` was removed. The ground-snap
threshold derives from `MaxAngleDelta.Sliding` instead of a `0.5` literal. `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation`
gained the `Correction.Enabled` gate its siblings already had. `applySurfaceNormal` was inlined and
`changedGrounded` renamed `changedContact`.

`ProbeGroundContact` is gated on the `applyCorrection` physics flag rather than on entity type.
`positionMatchesCachedPhysicsState` was extracted from `transformMatchesCachedPhysicsState`.

The entity literal gained `action`, `grounded`, `surfaceContact`, `surfaceNormal`, `alignedUp` and
`referenceNormal`; `createDefaultPlayerState` was de-duplicated against it. `jumpStartY` is now assigned
at jump time.

**Where**

[core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js),
[physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js),
[player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js),
[handlers/game/Enemy.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Enemy.js)

## Surface-relative movement, support-scaled deceleration, and the `Sliding` action

**What**

`UpdateMovement` no longer splits velocity on world XZ. It decomposes against `playerState.alignedUp` —
`normalVelocity = ScaleVector3(up, DotVector3(velocity, up))`, `tVel = SubtractVector3(velocity, normalVelocity)` —
runs acceleration, deceleration and clamping on `tVel`, and recombines with
`velocity.set(AddVector3(normalVelocity, tVel))`. `stoppingActive`, `getPrimaryOppositeHeld` and the
yaw-follows-momentum computation read an explicit XZ shadow literal and stay in the flat frame.

`getMovementDirection` takes an `up` parameter and returns a surface-projected `tangentDirection` alongside
the flat `direction`, built with `ProjectOntoPlane` from [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js) —
its first importer. Its JSDoc was corrected to the real signature and conditional return shape.

Deceleration magnitude is multiplied by `support = alignedUp.y` at both `ApplyDeceleration` call sites.

The jump launches along the surface normal: `velocity.set(AddVector3(tVel, ScaleVector3(up, launchSpeed)))`,
written before `SetPlayerAction("Jumping")`. The gate accepts `(grounded || onSlidingSurface)`, and
`solveJumpLaunchVelocity`'s return value is halved on a sliding surface.

`ResolvePlayerState` gained a `Sliding` branch between the underwater and airborne branches, keyed on
`surfaceContact === "sliding"`, with no exit rule. `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` adds `Math.PI / 2` to a
single `pitch` local consumed by both the change test and the rotation write.

**Where**

[player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js),
[physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js)

## Sliding state unified on `surfaceContact`, and per-medium angle limits

**What**

`ApplyGroundSnap` compares `Math.abs(deltaY) * normal.y` against `groundSnapTolerance` rather than
`Math.abs(deltaY)`, making the tolerance perpendicular instead of vertical. The resolved normal is hoisted
into a local shared with the steepness gate.

The sliding back-rotation in `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` keys on
`playerState.surfaceContact === "sliding"` instead of `playerState.action === "Sliding"`, and its offset is
`-Math.PI / 2` rather than `+Math.PI / 2`. In `ResolvePlayerState` the sliding branch moved above the
underwater branch.

`UpdateMovement` damps input that opposes the downslope direction while on a sliding surface, scaling
acceleration by 0.15; `onSlidingSurface` moved above the decomposition so both it and the jump gate share
one local. The downslope vector is `ProjectOntoPlane(WORLD_NORMALS.Down, up)`, left un-normalized. No-input
deceleration is additionally scaled by `controlMultiplier`.

`CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.MaxAngleDelta` split into `Air` and `Water` tables, each carrying `Ground`,
`Sliding` and `Recover`. A non-exported `angleLimitsFor(underwater)` selects between them and is read by
both `classifySurface` and the ground-snap steepness gate. `classifySurface` takes `underwater` as a
parameter.

**Where**

[physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js),
[player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Surface orientation solved from a full basis instead of frozen yaw

**What**

`computeAlignmentAngles` was replaced by `solveAlignmentRotation`, which builds an orthonormal
`(right, up, forward)` basis from `alignedUp` and the entity's heading and decomposes all three Euler
angles at once. `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` now writes the full triple through `rotation.set(solved)`,
and its pivot compensation spans yaw because both `before` and `after` are taken from the whole rotation.
The sliding back-rotation became a −90° rotation of the basis about its own right axis rather than a
constant added to a decomposed pitch.

The YXZ decomposition formulas were extracted out of `ComposeEulerRotations` into a shared
`decomposeEulerRows`, which gained a `degenerateRoll` parameter seeding the free angle at the pitch pole;
`ComposeEulerRotations` passes `0`. `EulerFromBasis` is a new exported basis-to-Euler entry point.

The forward axis fed to the basis is steered — heading from the entity's yaw, tilt carried from its
current forward axis. Its fallback chain is the uphill direction, then the flat heading when the surface
has no uphill.

**Where**

[math/Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js), [physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js)

## Surface-relative input from a carried tangent frame

**What**

`getMovementDirection` no longer flattens the camera basis to world XZ and projects that onto the surface
plane. Movement direction now comes from a carried tangent frame held per entity.

The entity literal gained `facing` — a world-space unit heading, initialised from the authored rotation
via `RotateByEuler(WORLD_NORMALS.Forward, rootTrans.rotation)` — and `inputFrame`, carrying
`carriedForward`, `previousCameraYaw`, `previousHasInput` and `previousGrounded`.

`player/Movement.js` gained `advanceCarriedForward`, which seeds the frame from the camera basis on a
no-input-to-input transition, on a change in `grounded`, and when transport collapses, and otherwise
composes the camera yaw delta with a re-projection onto the current surface plane. The seed is
`ProjectOntoPlane(camFwd, up)` plus an un-normalized uphill term weighted by `1 − |up.y|` and
`−dot(camFwd, up)`. `UpdateMovement` hoists the flattened camera basis and derives camera yaw as
`atan2(camFwd.x, camFwd.z)`; `direction` became the XZ shadow of `tangentDirection`; the three
previous-value fields are written unconditionally at the end of the function. A module constant
`minTangent` gates the collapse tests.

The `transform.rotation.y` write was removed. `turnFacingToward` rate-limits `facing` toward the
surface-tangential velocity direction at `momentumTurnRate`, reusing `moveAngleToward` through a 2D angle
taken in a basis built from `facing` itself. `solveAlignmentRotation` takes `facing` as a parameter,
which removed its sliding readback. `RespawnPlayer` resets `facing` and `inputFrame`.

**Where**

[player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js),
[builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js)

## Deceleration support floored, and a normalized flat camera forward

**What**

`support` in `UpdateMovement` is `Math.max(Math.abs(up.y), minSupport)` rather than a raw `up.y`, against
a new module constant `minSupport = 0.25`. It scales both `ApplyDeceleration` call sites — the
reverse-intent braking burst and the no-input decay.

The camera forward flattened to XZ is passed through `ResolveVector3Axis` at its hoist site, so it is unit
length where it previously carried `cos(pitch)`. It reaches `advanceCarriedForward`, the `cameraYaw`
derivation and `getPrimaryOppositeHeld` from there; `advanceCarriedForward`'s JSDoc dropped its
`un-normalized` note.

`handleEntityCollision` in testGame gates its spark burst on `detail.collision.result.includes("floor")`
in place of the removed `detail.groundContact`.

**Where**

[player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [testGame/main.js](engine/v1/testGame/main.js)

## Surface orientation split into an exact physics vector and an eased pose vector

**What**

The entity literal gained `poseUp` alongside `alignedUp`. `alignedUp` carries the exact target again —
world up when near-flat or contact-less, the surface normal otherwise — and is what every physics and
movement consumer reads. `poseUp` carries the rate-limited value and has a single reader:
`ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` passes it to `solveAlignmentRotation` in place of `alignedUp`.

`resetSurfaceState` and `ApplySurfaceCorrection` write both vectors, and their `changedOrientation` tests
the exact target and the eased pose together. `ApplySurfaceCorrection` captures `acquiring` from the
pre-write `surfaceContact` and passes `Math.PI` as the pose step on that frame, so the pose snaps on
contact acquisition and eases only between held contacts. `resetSurfaceState`'s release easing is
unchanged. `snapOrientationUpright` resets `poseUp`.

`CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.OrientationTurnRate` is 8, from 20.

**Where**

[physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js),
[player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Orientation easing moved from physics into a whole-model pose channel

**What**

`physics/` no longer eases. `poseUp` is gone from the entity literal and from `resetSurfaceState` and
`ApplySurfaceCorrection`, which now write `alignedUp` alone; the `acquiring` touchdown snap is gone; and
`ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` solves `transform.rotation` from `alignedUp`. Its pivot compensation is
gated on `surfaceContact !== "none"`. The exported `OrientationMaxStep` became
`ReferenceReleaseStep(deltaSeconds)`, reading a new `CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.ReferenceReleaseRate`;
`OrientationTurnRate` was removed. `physics/Master.js`'s `orientationStep` became `referenceStep` and
now feeds only the `referenceNormal` release.

`handlers/game/Animation.js` gained the model-pose channel: `buildModelPose`, `stepModelRotation`,
`resolveModelPose` and `resolvePoseStep`, plus a `walkModelParts` traversal helper that
`resolveAnimationStep` also uses. `resolveAnimationStep` takes a `root` parameter and seeds its walk with
it. `ResolveEntityAnimation` resolves the model pose first, then branches three ways: animated (walk from
the pose), idle-but-leaning (`clearDecorations`, then `resolvePoseStep`), idle and settled
(`clearDisplay`). `clearDisplay` split into `clearDecorations` and `clearPartDisplay`. The runtime gained
`modelPose`; `poseSettled` is an `EPSILON` comparison, not exact equality.

The entity literal's `orientationControl` became `modelTurnRate: { air, water }` in resolved
radians/second, against a module-private `defaultModelTurnRate`. `createDefaultPlayerState` scales it by
the character's `airControl` / `underwaterAirControl`. `snapOrientationUpright` clears
`animationRuntime` instead of resetting a pose vector.

**Where**

[handlers/game/Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js),
[physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js),
[builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js),
[core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [handlers/game/Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js)

## Model turn rate collapsed to one rate per entity

**What**

`modelTurnRate` on the entity literal is a single radians/second number rather than an
`{ air, water }` pair. `createDefaultPlayerState` resolves it as the builder default scaled by the
character's `airControl` alone. `resolveModelPose` reads `entity.modelTurnRate` directly, which removed
its `entity.underwater` read.

**Where**

[builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js),
[handlers/game/Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Model turn rate restored to a per-medium pair

**What**

Reverts the entry above; it does not describe the current source. `modelTurnRate` is again
`{ air, water }` on the entity literal, `createDefaultPlayerState` again scales the two halves by
`character.meta.airControl` and `character.meta.underwaterAirControl`, and `resolveModelPose` again
selects between them on `entity.underwater`.

**Where**

[builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js),
[handlers/game/Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)
